# WHAT IT CHANGES
#   dm/host/hle_thread.c:
#     * svc_thread_dump_live(): the existing state dump (svc_thread_dump) run under G (tried for 200 ms) with NO thread suspended (g_dump_live): each guest thread's wait, the object it waits
#       on, the guest stack of a thread in an SVC; a guest thread in NO guest wait also gets its scheduler flags and its host frames (host_frames: suspended only while its registers and
#       frame-pointer chain are copied, resumed before anything is printed); the host's own threads are listed the same way. (The old dump suspends threads for their backtraces; a thread
#       stopped while it holds the log's or the allocator's lock would stop the dump itself, which is why a live one is needed while the game is stuck.)
#     * a lock wait names its owner: by handle, or (SDK 22, Ocarina of Time's 22.2.8) by kernel ID, with its name.
#     * DM_THREAD_DUMP_AT=<seconds> (diagnostic, default unset): the live dump that many seconds after start.
#     * DM_QOS_MAP priority lending (the lock wait in svc_thread_impl): the owner is also looked up by kernel ID; before only by handle, which found none on SDK 22 games, so a user-
#       interactive main thread waiting for a lock whose owner ran at a lower QoS lent it nothing. THIS ONE IS A BEHAVIOUR CHANGE (only with g_qos_map, i.e. DM_QOS_MAP; the app's
#       default for it was not checked).
#   dm/gfx/nvn/hle_nvn.c:
#     * stall_watch(): a thread started at load. Once the game has presented 300 frames, a frame count unchanged for 5 s while graphics are not suspended logs
#       "[RED] stall: no frame for 5 s at frame N ..." and the live dump, once per stall, at most 4 times. DM_STALL_DUMP=0 turns it off. Default ON (reads one counter a second).
# What the fork's "5 s picture stop" report is: exactly this. It does not fix a freeze; it says which thread holds what (their L7.4 log: a game lock whose owner sat in host code with no CPU
#   for 28 s).
# Left out: the fork's front_ios.m part (the dump when the app goes to the background, and the 25 s background task for the pipeline archive's writes): front_ios.m is not in our host build
#   (load/front_*.m); the archive's writes at the end are engine-patches/0414's. The fork's t_dump_live test was not ported (it includes ../hle_thread.c with its own stubs).
# Shader chain: not touched. Checked: patch -p1 --forward --dry-run, no fuzz, on the tree + 0401..0415 + 0500, 0503; hle_thread.c and hle_nvn.c pass clang -fsyntax-only (the host's
#   include paths, profile 010015100B514000, Super Mario Bros. Wonder). NOT run, NOT run on a device.
# Use: nothing to set (watchdog on). DM_STALL_DUMP=0 to turn it off; DM_THREAD_DUMP_AT=120 for a dump 2 minutes in.

